{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What to do with an AAGUID that has no MDS entry (i.e. FIDO Alliance has no metadata for it —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not necessarily malicious, MDS coverage is incomplete for some legitimate authenticators)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnknownAaguidAction"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"open","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including the records the caller did ask for."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own raw value is the empty string, which no server value is, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" is never written: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" refuses it locally, before any request, as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validation failure (CONTRACT.md §34.2 P12.2, contract 1.60 A4) — never as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"\""},{"type":"text","text":", never left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the server to refuse. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" over these cases needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" arm."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/unknownaaguidaction"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK19UnknownAaguidActionO","symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnknownAaguidAction"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnknownAaguidAction"}],"title":"UnknownAaguidAction"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UnknownAaguidAction"},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UnknownAaguidAction\/allow","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UnknownAaguidAction\/deny","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UnknownAaguidAction\/unknown"],"title":"Enumeration Cases","anchor":"Enumeration-Cases"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UnknownAaguidAction\/init(from:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UnknownAaguidAction\/init(rawValue:)"],"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UnknownAaguidAction\/encode(to:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UnknownAaguidA